A messenger once carried precious cargo between two distant kingdoms. Her route passed through Echo Cave, where a guardian spirit dwelt who could multiply any offering left at the threshold.

The kingdoms had long been isolated, but famine threatened. The messenger arrived with three sacks of grain from her homeland—more than half their reserves, but not everything. It was enough to show commitment, yet prudent enough to preserve something if trust proved misplaced.

She placed the sacks at the cave's entrance. The echo spirit's voice resonated: "I shall triple what you've brought. But I cannot force the kingdom beyond to share the bounty fairly. That choice belongs to them."

